{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread","id":1415331,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade: Night Road discussion thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-24T15:24:32-07:00","id":1415331,"title":"Vampire: The Masquerade: Night Road discussion thread","content":"<img src=\"https://cdn.cloudflare.steamstatic.com/steam/apps/1290270/header.jpg?t=1600950700\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Steam: <a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1290270/Vampire_The_Masquerade__Night_Road/\" target=\"_blank\">https://store.steampowered.com/app/1...e__Night_Road/</a><br /> <br /> TV tropes Page: <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/VideoGame/VampireTheMasqueradeNightRoad\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...eradeNightRoad</a><br /> <br /> The text-based adventure is one that came out today and I'm pleased to say that I've finished two playthroughs, though the second one didn't work out great. I am really going to be interested in what people think of this as it's not even a visual novel but a literal &quot;choose your own adventure&quot; one with a little artwork. On the other hand, the storytelling is top notch and it offers a lot more choices than the Visual Novels did.<br /> <br /> The premise is you're a Courier for the Camarilla after having been Embraced a couple of years ago. You got some genuinely horrifying and shit jobs in the prior years (like feeding undocumented immigrants to Elders) but have since moved up to being a driver. Now you have a chance of playing against a tech bro super-genius Anarch who wants to SAVE THE VAMPIRE RACE via STEM and a traditionalist but mostly good hearted(ish) Camarilla Prince who was once friends with the Bloodlines protagonist. The Second Inquisition is at their most terrifying this time and you have to constantly dodge them this game.<br /> <br /> Feeding, Humanity, and Keeping the Masquerade is always important. Also, what you can do is determined by your stats.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T01:29:33-07:00","id":1415371,"title":"","content":"Night Road is a very good much nice great game. It has a big problem with bugs and typos though.<br /> <br /> Throwing down with thaumaturgy against a true mage was fun (except for the bugs). It makes me sad though that V5 is not like that. Characters in V5 are not cool like this, don't have broad and interesting powers like this protagonist, and are all around juts less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T03:46:26-07:00","id":1415389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1415371#post1415371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night Road is a very good much nice great game. It has a big problem with bugs and typos though.<br /> <br /> Throwing down with thaumaturgy against a true mage was fun (except for the bugs). It makes me sad though that V5 is not like that. Characters in V5 are not cool like this, don't have broad and interesting powers like this protagonist, and are all around juts less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that if you use V5's setting and rules to make a game for V5 then you are V5.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I felt that it was perhaps a little TOO accurate with its handling of Hunger. You rack up Hunger way too fast and it took me awhile to learn to manage it with quite the body count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T06:37:07-07:00","id":1415405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1415389#post1415389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that if you use V5's setting and rules to make a game for V5 then you are V5.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I felt that it was perhaps a little TOO accurate with its handling of Hunger. You rack up Hunger way too fast and it took me awhile to learn to manage it with quite the body count.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 rules, such as using Dominate on animals and vampires of lower generations, having Perdo Magica, and having Auspex help with shooting.<br /> Night Road is much closer to FATE mechanics. Protagonist's dots in disciplines are more of a proficiency with the general domain governed by the discipline than the rigid powers of V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T13:09:12-07:00","id":1415452,"title":"","content":"<b>My review of Night Road</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/09/vampire-masquerade-night-road-review.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/09/vampire-masquerade-night-road-review.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/09/vampire-masquerade-night-road-review.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2020/09/vampire-masquerade-night-road-review.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Warning - This review contains minor spoilers for the first half of Night Road.<br /> <br /> Vampire: The Masquerade: Night Road by Choice of Game is a text-based choose your own adventure game. It's not even a visual novel with the entirety of the game being text with a scattered few character portraits. It's the kind of game you would play on your cellphone but that doesn't mean it's not deep. The writing is far deeper and, ironically, allows a great deal more freedom in determining your character's choices. It also incorporates the tabletop games' rules regarding Hunger, Humanity, the Masquerade, and skill sets.<br /> <br /> How good is the writing? It's a rare game that allows me to have a character arc for my video game protagonist. However, the character I created for this game, Ransom, is a guy who started as a duplicitous and self-interested scumbag before making turnaround due to seeing the true depravity of his fellow Kindred. He killed two innocents during feeding, killed his sire, rescued a bunch of migrant workers from blood slavery, fell in love, played genius vampires against one another, and finally decided to just get the hell out of town. On my second playthrough, I didn't repeat any of those actions and had a lot more choices to go through.<br /> <br /> The premise is that you are a vampire who has been able to survive his first few years as an undead predator. This automatically makes you different from the protagonists of most Vampire: The Masquerade media. You aren't the absolute rock bottom of Kindred society but a respected(ish) professional doing a necessary service for the Camarilla. Being a courier is different from being Sheriff or Scourge but at least you can expect to actually be paid for your work.<br /> <br /> The situation in the Tuscon, Arizona is pretty bad for Kindred. The Second Inquisition has got electronic surveillance on large numbers of the undead, has driven the undead of Dallas, and is seemingly everywhere. The current Prince, Lettow, doesn't trust cellphones or other modern conveniences and he's not necessarily wrong. His predecessor supported large numbers of mad science experiments including cloning blood and trying to enhance Kindred abilities. This has brought massive attention to the undead in the region.<br /> <br /> Contrasting Lettow is the perky Anarch tech bro, Julian, who has grand visions of a future defined by transvampirism as well as a controlled crash of the Masquerade. In a society where everyone has a cellphone, there's no possibility of keeping the existence of vampires secret. You'd need some sort of all-pervasive magical Technocracy to do that (and vampires don't know that exists). He believes STEM and a controlled propaganda campaign are the only way to pave the way for human-vampire coexistence.<br /> <br /> Your character is caught between these two individuals and their competing visions for the future of the vampire race. Lettow is about as reasonable a Prince as can be imagined in the setting, possibly because he's Gangrel rather than Ventrue, and even mentions being a friend to the protagonist from Bloodlines. Julian is shown to be a friend of your character early on. However, his ambitions are running up against the fact that vampires are monsters and it's very easy to kill innocent people even if you're trying to be a &quot;good&quot; one. Interestingly, enough, night-to-night survival is just as much an issue as the behind-the-scenes business of being undead. You begin the game with no haven, no car, no money, and no wheels.<br /> <br /> Let's just say you had a bad night in the desert. You also are starving and everyone around you looks good but feeding could result in you killing. It requires making contacts and playing your cards right to get equipped to do the jobs necessary to make money. The feeling of desperation is one that I didn't expect and is very appropriate for V5. Your Kindred can even say, multiple times, you are only in this for the money.<br /> <br /> Being a text-based game is both the game's biggest strength as well as biggest weakness. The lion's share of the game requires you to use your imagination to fill in the blanks. We're partying like it's 1988 with those books that came with Sierra software games like Wasteland. Even then, that had actual characters on the screen and gameplay. Still, I found it remarkably easy to get into this as a text-based RPG. The fact they don't have to limit themselves to what is programmable means that they have far more freedom to describe whatever they want. Like a novel, the only limit is one's imagination.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the gameplay is the closest to the actual tabletop game. If you try and Intimidate someone but don't have a very high Manipulation or Intimidate score, you're going to fail. If you're not very good with guns, you're going to miss. Much of the game depends on you spending your experience judiciously between social, combat, supernatural, and academic abilities. Virtually every level gives you a half-dozen ways of approaching things and you can't do them all. Disciplines also rouse your Hunger and managing that is far more difficult than I imagined. Some of the best parts of the game are accidentally killing a human and then being forced to dispose of their body.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that Night Road takes some jabs at current politics in America. One of the levels is an overcrowded hospital where the conditions are horrifying (made worse by Kindred feeding) but that's because it's the only free hospital in the area. Another level has hundreds of migrants gathered in a slave pit where they are regularly bled for the sale of their blood to vampires in Seattle. The Second Inquisition is also implied to be as powerful as it is because it's leaching off the excessive amount of surveillance and personnel watching the Mexican border.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, this is a solid game if you don't mind a lot of reading. It's dark, gritty, violent, and horrifying. It's definitely a game for adults with multiple sex scenes and plenty of hard moral choices. I admit, I kind of regret that this wasn't a Triple A game or even a AA because it does have the kind of plot that would have made an awesome Bloodlines spin off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-25-2020, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-25T21:48:03-07:00","id":1415503,"title":"","content":"The greatest moment of Night Road is when Elena, an undocumented immigrant, dressed up in cosplay of Neil Patrick Harris' Space Nazi to befriend some Russian Brujah white supremacists.<br /> <br /> &quot;Didn't the Nazis hate the Slavs?&quot;<br /> <br /> It is so incredibly random and awesome that it is something I had to re-read twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T05:49:08-07:00","id":1415526,"title":"","content":"I have only two criticisms of the game:<br /> 1. It's buggy as hell. Sometimes the stat modifiers are wrong. Sometimes the option gates are wrong. Sometimes the entire scene chunks are skipped (ending of the fight with Mage).<br /> 2. Maybe I've just read things wrong, but I felt mislead by the sales pitch. I expected a road adventure as you attempt to do your delivery. But the actual structure of the game is several independent missions connected to an interlude hub, and the actual deliveries feel almost like an afterthought.<br /> <br /> It's a very good game, and for the most part, I've enjoyed it. There's a lot of smoke and mirrors going on to hide the linear nature of the game, but I'd still easily recommend it to anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T06:24:46-07:00","id":1415528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1415526#post1415526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only two criticisms of the game:<br /> 1. It's buggy as hell. Sometimes the stat modifiers are wrong. Sometimes the option gates are wrong. Sometimes the entire scene chunks are skipped (ending of the fight with Mage).<br /> 2. Maybe I've just read things wrong, but I felt mislead by the sales pitch. I expected a road adventure as you attempt to do your delivery. But the actual structure of the game is several independent missions connected to an interlude hub, and the actual deliveries feel almost like an afterthought.<br /> <br /> It's a very good game, and for the most part, I've enjoyed it. There's a lot of smoke and mirrors going on to hide the linear nature of the game, but I'd still easily recommend it to anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. You can fight a mage in the game? Really? How? Where?<br /> <br /> 2. There is a single mission where you have to deliver a package to a plane taking off on a runway while the Inquisition plus several car chases. I thought the deliveries were just an excuse to involve you in Kindred affairs, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T10:03:08-07:00","id":1415568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1415528#post1415528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. You can fight a mage in the game? Really? How? Where?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">During the mission with Dr. Caul, you need to make Vani into a potential ally and have her survive the mission. This will let you visit her after the mission and make her your ghoul. Vani tells you that she's being haunted by Giselle, Caul's ghouled verbena, because Giselle is in withdrawal and mad with envy. So you have a throwdown with Giselle, who is an extremely powerful mage by the look of it. One of the options is to lure her into a sciency area to disrupt her magic. The other is to do a direct competition of her magic versus your Blood Sorcery:<br /> <a href=\"https://pastebin.com/mA77QMbX\" target=\"_blank\">https://pastebin.com/mA77QMbX</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T14:09:28-07:00","id":1415597,"title":"","content":"how long is the game? (roughly)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T15:28:20-07:00","id":1415612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1415597#post1415597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how long is the game? (roughly)</div> </div> </div> </div>4-8 hours depending on your speed of reading as well as choices.<br /> <br /> Mind you, Huddy is doing a playthrough and she's 4 hours in without even having finished the first third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T16:33:54-07:00","id":1553272,"title":"","content":"I'm enjoying playing this game, just have a few problems with it (very minor spoilers ahead).<br /> <br /> 1. Julian is kind of a Mary Sue and it's fucking annoying, he's so idiotic and disgusting that makes me want to kill him, but it seems it's hard to do so, because everything works for him.<br /> <br /> 2. Mortals and ghouls are way stronger than they should be, I tried to feed on a waiter after charming him with my bissexual Tremere and the dude got scared and was able to throw a fucking bookshelf on me and ran away before I had a chance to do anything about it. I tried to kill Julian's ghoul and the bitch still managed to shoot me and ran away. I really got mad at that lol.<br /> <br /> 3. Hunger is a bit too harsh imo, can't really rely on disciplines as often as I think we should. Still, I liked what we can do with our disciplines, it's much more open than with V5 and imo the game (tabletop) would be much more interesting if disciplines were as open as this, prhaps not as open as True Magick, but at least a bit more open is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-19T16:36:59-07:00","id":1553273,"title":"","content":"Some of the bane reworks are bland. Gangrel has one of the most fun banes in the tabletop version. The Night Road version is a bland dice penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-20T01:24:18-07:00","id":1553278,"title":"","content":"I'm getting really disappointed tbh, I'm starving and charm a woman, she comes with me, start to kiss, etc. she says &quot;it's crazy&quot;I'm alone with her, I have a fucking sword and a gun and &quot;she goes away&quot;, there's no option to feed, I mean wtf!? A moment before it was with another mortal, I mean this is the kind of thing that wouldn't really happen on tabletop and it's fucking annoying, it seems Parliament of Knives will remain my favourite of these games. The lack of options to feed, do anything violent/crazy, because oh well you're starving, is really disappointing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T05:43:09-07:00","id":1553395,"title":"","content":"Damn! People now only talk about Bloodlines 2 and it seems not many people around here played Night Road...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-23T14:27:44-07:00","id":1553409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553395#post1553395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn! People now only talk about Bloodlines 2 and it seems not many people around here played Night Road...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been following and reading your posts on it, but I'm not a text-based game kind of girl, so I didn't really played this or any other VtM game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-24T10:05:04-07:00","id":1553428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553409#post1553409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been following and reading your posts on it, but I'm not a text-based game kind of girl, so I didn't really played this or any other VtM game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh I wasn't a text-based game kind of boy, but then I suddenly became kind of addicted to the ones released for VtM. Shadows of New York and Parliament of Knives are by far my favourites. If you want to give it a try, I'd tell you to start with the graphic novels of New York, Coteries of New York and Shadows of New York, I think you might enjoy them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-25T07:54:44-07:00","id":1553440,"title":"","content":"I'd give the game an 8 out of 10<br /> <br /> I like the &quot;choice of game&quot; style, and this one is the currently best vtm one.<br /> <br /> For the positives<br /> <br /> Interesting plot<br /> <br /> While the game has a set direction, there's variety in how each situation can be accimplished<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThere's hidden unique situations, such as a potential friendship with a hunter if you make specific actions in the prologue<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For the negatives<br /> <br /> Minor shades:<br /> <br /> The character creations gives us a lot of personnalisation for our background, but it doesn't matter in the long run. As a tremere, Dr caul could have embraced me as a help on her quest to regain the lost magehood of the tremere, or to mix thaumaturge with advanced science, and that never comes into the game, even when I meet her again. Same for the ravnos site.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also advise anyone to play in the gm mode which allows you to see which characteristics are rolled.<br /> <br /> Biggest issues<br /> <br /> The game is very long. Which is not be a problem in itself, except if you want to try finding out specific routes, you have to do aaaaaaaaaaaaalllllllll it. And even while ignoring the reading what you already known, it takes a hell of a long time. The game would really, REALLY benefit from a save system. Or a selectable chapter system. Especially since the achievement list give you incentive to replay the game.<br /> <br /> And most importantly.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Fucking julian<br /> <br /> In my first playthrought it was bearable, since I was interested in his plot was going.<br /> <br /> But afterward he's untolerable, you can't ever get him to shut up, no matter how much you try you can't avoid his dialogues, it feels like a writer's favorite, and as said above, he is a textbook Gary stue.<br /> <br /> The &quot;betraying the kindred for the second inquisition&quot; was worth it just for his reaction to the bretrayal and the chance to end him.<br /> <br /> The game would en a straight out 9/10 if we could get Julian to just shut up for the majority of the plot and only appear when his plot is relevant at the end","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","user":"Nyremne","date":". 08-25-2025, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-26T16:37:01-07:00","id":1553473,"title":"","content":"I am divided on this game.<br /> <br /> On the positives<br /> <br /> Big clan selection Including game altering ones like Caitiff and Malkavian.<br /> <br /> Low humanity actually makes you more monstrous, in mentality and feeling.<br /> <br /> Picking to perpetuate your existence and accepting what you are, and the like actually has effects.<br /> <br /> I can kill most of the people that annoy me and am given many opportunities to lie.<br /> <br /> Negatives<br /> <br /> Hunger is far too limiting as far as I can tell even though I do not like V5 you are supposed to get rouse checks but it seems as if your character just fails almost every rouse check meaning every use of an ability almost always increases your hunger. This is basically like being a thinblood in v20. As you with a blood pool of five are equivalent to a thin blood with a pool of ten due to their doubled blood cost. This is even more egregious since your character is of a respectable generation 11th. Lower for Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Disciplines in general feel rather weak especially the social ones, if you spec for a social character you are better off just using social abilities than presence or dominate, which sort of defeats a big part of the point of having them... Using disciplines alongside your social skills should give you even better outcomes, especially presence yet they really do not seem to most of the time.<br /> <br /> Julian, by the dark father I utterly despise him, every time he shows up I long to end him. The fact that you can only kill him in one ending and that ending requires you to fully betray your own kind irks me endlessly. He is a Masquerade risk, and worse than that he is a horrifically manipulative little leech, the fact that no one tries to kill him at all makes me suspect he was the author's little pet. (Sort of like Beckett if I am honest. Though far more annoying.) The type of characters I play would never associate with someone like him shared past or no.<br /> <br /> Diablerie, I have nothing against Caine's loophole but forcing the player to play a diablerist is certainly an interesting take. Especially with how whiny and repentant the character seems to be at game start? Like from the background options given I cannot understand why the character even committed Diablerie if they were going to whine about it so much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T02:07:00-07:00","id":1553476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553473#post1553473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie, I have nothing against Caine's loophole but forcing the player to play a diablerist is certainly an interesting take. Especially with how whiny and repentant the character seems to be at game start? Like from the background options given I cannot understand why the character even committed Diablerie if they were going to whine about it so much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they necessarily had a choice in the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T10:04:26-07:00","id":1553484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553476#post1553476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think they necessarily had a choice in the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to see you are still active first of all.<br /> <br /> I have to replay it, I cannot recall if they did or not have a choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> Though even if you just accidentally bury your teeth into another kindreds neck, even when under frenzy if memory serves a kindred's beast will not commit diablerie as once the easily accessible vitae is lost it requires additional rolls. Diablerie is ALWAYS a conscious act as far as I can find, now I will admit I do not know if V5 changed this but in 20th and earlier that seems to universally be the case, even way back in first and second edition Diablerie was a conscious choice.<br /> <br /> Personally, second edition was my favorite with the rules of Diablerie, as by the time we got to revised the consequences of diablerie often made it more trouble than it was worth. It also invalidated or made certain paths nonsensical by just making it way too great a risk to be a tenet of a path.<br /> <br /> <br /> To further this argument.<br /> <br /> After sucking down the last of the blood, but before the delicious soul starts being drained away, there is a contest of sorts involving strength. During this contest, there is NO more blood, so any hunger frenzy will see any further drinking as useless. The vampire will also stop fighting back before the soul gets involved, (after it gets involved is another story) so anger frenzy isn't going to be an excuse. Fear frenzy doesn't even make sense regarding diablerie. You can't diablerize in self-defense. You can definitely drain a kindred of all blood and put them into torpor out of a frenzy or hunger but Diablerie is several steps further than that.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T11:05:18-07:00","id":1553487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553484#post1553484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good to see you are still active first of all.<br /> <br /> I have to replay it, I cannot recall if they did or not have a choice in the matter.<br /> <br /> Though even if you just accidentally bury your teeth into another kindreds neck, even when under frenzy if memory serves a kindred's beast will not commit diablerie as once the easily accessible vitae is lost it requires additional rolls. Diablerie is ALWAYS a conscious act as far as I can find, now I will admit I do not know if V5 changed this but in 20th and earlier that seems to universally be the case, even way back in first and second edition Diablerie was a conscious choice.<br /> <br /> Personally, second edition was my favorite with the rules of Diablerie, as by the time we got to revised the consequences of diablerie often made it more trouble than it was worth. It also invalidated or made certain paths nonsensical by just making it way too great a risk to be a tenet of a path.<br /> <br /> To further this argument.<br /> <br /> After sucking down the last of the blood, but before the delicious soul starts being drained away, there is a contest of sorts involving strength. During this contest, there is NO more blood, so any hunger frenzy will see any further drinking as useless. The vampire will also stop fighting back before the soul gets involved, (after it gets involved is another story) so anger frenzy isn't going to be an excuse. Fear frenzy doesn't even make sense regarding diablerie. You can't diablerize in self-defense. You can definitely drain a kindred of all blood and put them into torpor out of a frenzy or hunger but Diablerie is several steps further than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi, yeah, I still drop in every few weeks.<br /> <br /> WOD has just been such a big influence on my writing that it's hard to quit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's a rule I'm unfamiliar with and diablerie as a accident was something that happened a lot in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T11:55:15-07:00","id":1553489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553487#post1553487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hi, yeah, I still drop in every few weeks.<br /> <br /> WOD has just been such a big influence on my writing that it's hard to quit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That's a rule I'm unfamiliar with and diablerie as a accident was something that happened a lot in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha I feel that! I used to mostly lurk here for years made an account and still I mostly just lurk, channeling my inner Malk I guess.<br /> <br /> Same... I mostly just cannot escape vampires, be it Masquerade or Requiem.<br /> <br /> I am not quite sure if it is hard or fast but most references to Diablerie say something about the vampire choosing to commit the act, Requiem as far as I can recall explicitly spells out that the vampire's beast will not commit diablerie. Could be mistaken as I have read and played quite a few different books and games over the years.<br /> <br /> I think the act has to be conscious for a couple reasons.<br /> <br /> 1 in first and second edition it is presented as a choice.<br /> <br /> &quot;If a character wishes to continue drinking the blood of a vampiric vessel, even after all the blood is drained, he must roll Strength against a difficulty of nine. Each success indicates that the target loses one Health Level. No blood is actually drained, but instead the very spirit of the vampire is taken from the body. Once all the vessel's Health Levels have been taken, she dies the Final Death, and her life-force is passed along to the character. If the vessel was not of an earlier generation, this does not mean very much. Such cannot be done with monals, for their life-forces have already been extinguished by the time they lose all their Blood Points.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2 Revised has this to say<br /> <br /> &quot;Once a vampire\u2019s body has been drained of all blood, the<br /> true struggle begins. The diablerist\u2019s player makes an extended<br /> Strength roll (difficulty 9). Each success inflicts one automatic<br /> health level on the victim (the victim cannot soak, and damage<br /> is considered aggravated). When all the victim\u2019s health levels<br /> have been drained, the victim\u2019s essence is taken into the attacker<br /> and the emptied body begins decaying immediately.<br /> A vampire committing diablerie is quite vulnerable to<br /> attack. Total concentration goes into the struggle to draw forth<br /> the essence of the victim, and stopping for even a moment ruins<br /> the chance of capturing the spirit. All attacks against a vampire<br /> attempting diablerie are made versus a difficulty of 2.<br /> <br /> Upon successful completion of diablerie, the diablerist is<br /> overwhelmed by euphoria, and a Self-control roll is necessary<br /> (difficulty 10 minus the character\u2019s Humanity) to avoid frenzy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note the text saying to avoid Frenzy, why would this be included if one could diablerize in a frenzy? <br /> <br /> <br /> All this being said there is one character I know of who supposedly diablerized while under the Frenzy Al-Hakim from Jerusalem by Night. There may be more in other books, but as I said I do not have everything.<br /> <br /> Though I would argue much like the existence of other weirdness in the fluff like humanity zero vampires functioning not as wights and entire cities being blood bonded through wells, that mechanics and fluff do not always mix 1 to 1. <br /> <br /> So if you want to have frenzy make diablerie possible for drama I say go ahead, as some stuff does back it up. I just believe that the hunger frenzy would not justify it (no more vitae) the rage frenzy would view it as too slow and would rather kill the thing ticking it off as fast as possible (diablerie takes a good amount of time and a number of rolls) and the fear frenzy doesn't make much sense for it.<br /> <br /> These are of course my beliefs.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T14:04:41-07:00","id":1553493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553484#post1553484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, second edition was my favorite with the rules of Diablerie, as by the time we got to revised the consequences of diablerie often made it more trouble than it was worth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strange, AFAIR the extra rules were still optional. I kept using standard rules, anyway (you lose Humanity and risks Addiction, that's mostly it).<br /> <br /> But I'm almost sure you're right that it has to be a conscious act. I really don't remember the rule ever, in any edition, giving room for someone to avoid losing the Humanity dot, and I think not being able to do it without a conscious choice was a big part of it. I may be mistake, though.<br /> <br /> Of course, the lore doesn't always follows the rules, so if the game's character did it... ok.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T18:06:47-07:00","id":1553496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553493#post1553493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Strange, AFAIR the extra rules were still optional. I kept using standard rules, anyway (you lose Humanity and risks Addiction, that's mostly it).<br /> <br /> But I'm almost sure you're right that it has to be a conscious act. I really don't remember the rule ever, in any edition, giving room for someone to avoid losing the Humanity dot, and I think not being able to do it without a conscious choice was a big part of it. I may be mistake, though.<br /> <br /> Of course, the lore doesn't always follows the rules, so if the game's character did it... ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I assumed the Humanity Loss is because absorbing someone else's soul was going to fuck you up no matter what.<br /> <br /> I also made Humanity losses for frenzy murders regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T18:08:01-07:00","id":1553497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553489#post1553489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I would argue much like the existence of other weirdness in the fluff like humanity zero vampires functioning not as wights and entire cities being blood bonded through wells, that mechanics and fluff do not always mix 1 to 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Humanity 0 thing was primarily a first edition thing where it wasn't that you became a Wight (which came later) but the fact that you became an NPC and irredeemably evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T19:17:51-07:00","id":1553500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553496#post1553496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I assumed the Humanity Loss is because absorbing someone else's soul was going to fuck you up no matter what.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a problem with this interpretation, I just don't think that was what I saw. But I won't verify for now, I'm without my books here, and it won't make a lot of a difference.<br /> <br /> That's something that will impact more your games' themes than any important mechanic, so to each their own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553497#post1553497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the Humanity 0 thing was primarily a first edition thing where it wasn't that you became a Wight (which came later) but the fact that you became an NPC and irredeemably evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if either that was the case or if there was a Humanity 0 Vampire so described in later editions.<br /> <br /> But we do have things like Kemintiri being brought back from Wightdom, which should be simply impossible, or Sobek becoming an Abomination, which also should be simply impossible.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, whenever Set is involved, directly or not, we have a lot of impossible things happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T19:49:41-07:00","id":1553504,"title":"","content":"Not letting me quote you for some reason apologies. I hope you see this.<br /> <br /> Humanity zero has as far as I can understand it always been complete loss of self to the beast. Wight is not the correct term for first edition I admit it was one of the terms used for referring to mortals in that edition.<br /> <br /> Granted it is important to note that the beast was different in first edition.<br /> <br /> A couple excerpts from first edition.<br /> <br /> &quot;Humanity: The amount of Humanity a Vampire possesses is vitally important to the character. Vampires need to retain their sense of humanness as much as possible or grow more distant from the human world and thus from their own roots. The less human they become, the more monstrous they get. Eventually, they lose track of what they are and have no means of keeping in touch with any other aspect of their nature but the Beast within.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wassail The Final release and the last Frenzy .<br /> Occurs when the last vestiges of Humanity are lost and a Vampire plunges into a world of chaos.&quot;<br /> <br /> And most notably.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Beast is symbolic of the dark side of the human spirit, the shadow (Jung's word for the suppressed darker half).&quot;<br /> <br /> You are still losing yourself, but it is not to some bestial incarnate of Caine's rage, but rather you have fallen to your shadow, the twisted reflection of yourself made manifest and sentient via the embrace. You are not evil; you are technically just not you anymore since the symbolic Shadow has taken control.<br /> <br /> This actually very important since Golconda originally involved accepting the beast/shadow as a part of yourself in order to stop it from taking you over.<br /> <br /> &quot;Once Golconda has been reached, you are at peace with yourself. You no longer exist in a life filled with self-horror and self-pity. You have finally mastered the Beast within by<br /> accepting that the Beast is a part of you. There is only one major benefit for having reached Golconda, but this one is enough. When a Vampire reaches Golconda, they no longer Frenzy. No Frenzy rolls need ever be made for as long as they remain in Golconda.&quot;<br /> <br /> Later editions made the Beast mindless, but that was not the intent of first edition you are correct on that. However, you are also technically no longer yourself at humanity zero. Mindless you may not be, but you are effectively gone I would argue.<br /> <br /> The sabbat in first edition were not very fleshed out and were listed as humanity zero but what would become paths/roads were hinted at in the original Storyteller's handbook.<br /> <br /> &quot;However, members of the Sabbat seem capable of their own kind of virtues. They possess an intense loyalty to one another. Indeed, among more knowledgeable members of the Camarilla, rumors fly regarding Sabbat mystics, who spend their unlives in quests after knowledge about the history of the Kindred. (Path of Caine?) Others talk about honorable Sabbat leaders who strive desperately to keep the Vampiric world from going up in smoke. (Path of honorable accord?) Some members of the Camarilla even whisper that greatest of heresies -that there may be much the Camarilla can learn from its eternal enemies.&quot; (Path/road system in general?)<br /> <br /> And brainwashing after stripping humanity is clearly listed in the core book. (The central step of entering a path/road?)<br /> <br /> &quot;Their initiation procedure is designed to destroy any of the vestigial will in a new Vampire. The Initiates are slain, slowly and painfully, and then given the Blood. This Blood doesn't come from one member of the Sabbat, but from as many as are present at the initiation, combined into a chalice. Once the Initiate has been given the Blood, he is buried alive. He must crawl out in order to live. Those who do not, spend eternity buried under the earth. The process of digging oneself from a Chapter Seven: Setting grave tears the Initiate's Humanity from him and opens him to the Subjugation and brainwashing of the Sabbat.&quot;<br /> <br /> God, I miss the original creation rites. Though this form of mass embrace caused a lot of Caitiff it being tied to the Vaulderie was cool, thematic, and very monstrous. Suitable for their original role as antagonists.<br /> <br /> On another subject the humanity zero characters I was referencing were from second edition Berlin by Night. A rather distasteful book but one I do possess. This is notable because this book came out after the formal creation of paths. Even if they did not have the paths/roads done for all of the clans/sects listing them as humanity 0 is a huge mistake. One of them was Kemintiri who was actually even brought back from being a wight if I remember right.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is fun! You are giving me a reason to reread the old books again.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-27T21:49:23-07:00","id":1553506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553504#post1553504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not letting me quote you for some reason apologies. I hope you see this.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use @ when that happens. The Quote function has some bugs that take time and uses to get used to.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> read the post above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553504#post1553504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast is symbolic of the dark side of the human spirit, the shadow (Jung's word for the suppressed darker half).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that's not how Jung's Shadow work at all, their idea is more similar to Freud's Id. This comparison has the problem of causing more confusion than explaining if the reader tries to learn about it.<br /> <br /> And with their description of Wassail, seriously, the distinction is mostly semantics.<br /> <br /> With the kind of personality described (call it Beast, Shadow or Id), one of the results is a complete lack of impulse control. That may not be a person deprived of reason, or in constant Frenzy, but is a person who never waits before taking what they want and utterly incapable of dealing with frustration.<br /> <br /> This kind of person does exist, by the way. They're the most severe cases of Psychopathy, very rare and very stupid, sometimes also very dangerous, although not necessarily so. They may be brilliant people and capable of long term planing, but their absolute absence of emotional intelligence and resilience does make them non-functional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BloodyRelight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553504#post1553504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of them was Kemintiri who was actually even brought back from being a wight if I remember right.</div> </div> </div> </div>She was retconned to have been brought back from Wassail still in ancient Egypt, but yeah. Her Humanity is still very low, but exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-28T14:15:52-07:00","id":1553523,"title":"","content":"I see the post above, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-09T01:58:41-08:00","id":1557407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1553428#post1553428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tbh I wasn't a text-based game kind of boy, but then I suddenly became kind of addicted to the ones released for VtM. Shadows of New York and Parliament of Knives are by far my favourites. If you want to give it a try, I'd tell you to start with the graphic novels of New York, Coteries of New York and Shadows of New York, I think you might enjoy them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I recommend Parliament of Knives, but strongly discourage people from the New York trilogy.<br /> <br /> Parliament of Knives is written by the same guy who did the Werewolves series, which I also enjoyed. Not only does the game not brow beat you over the head by TELLING you how your character is supposed to be feeling about a particular situation / action (unlike New York), but the DLC also lets you join the Sabbat in one of the endings.<br /> <br /> <br /> New York, on the other hand, your choices do not matter. Even if you fuck up royal and fail to assemble a coterie, the game will still bail you out at the end when you get into trouble. It's railroaded to hell and back, as if you try to do something the Storyteller disapproves of, it will seize control of your character and force you back on track.<br /> <br /> The third game in the series is probably the worst, as I've seen people report about how it completely disregarded their choices made in previous chapters, in order to present a 'canon' route for its plot. Characters who had died in previous games suddenly coming back to life, as if nothing happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-13T16:07:55-08:00","id":1557565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557407#post1557407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I recommend Parliament of Knives, but strongly discourage people from the New York trilogy.<br /> <br /> Parliament of Knives is written by the same guy who did the Werewolves series, which I also enjoyed. Not only does the game not brow beat you over the head by TELLING you how your character is supposed to be feeling about a particular situation / action (unlike New York), but the DLC also lets you join the Sabbat in one of the endings.<br /> <br /> <br /> New York, on the other hand, your choices do not matter. Even if you fuck up royal and fail to assemble a coterie, the game will still bail you out at the end when you get into trouble. It's railroaded to hell and back, as if you try to do something the Storyteller disapproves of, it will seize control of your character and force you back on track.<br /> <br /> The third game in the series is probably the worst, as I've seen people report about how it completely disregarded their choices made in previous chapters, in order to present a 'canon' route for its plot. Characters who had died in previous games suddenly coming back to life, as if nothing happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoy them both, but for very different reasons. I agree with you about the lack of choice in the New York games. I am very clear that they are Visual Novels with little &quot;game&quot; there, while the Choice of Games line are all pretty good interactive fiction games. I think a lot of the charm of the New York games is that (with the exception of the third one) they are pretty good at creating an atmosphere that a lot of people have vibed on. The art is really evocative, even if the story is a railroad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T06:00:40-08:00","id":1557674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557407#post1557407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I recommend Parliament of Knives, but strongly discourage people from the New York trilogy.<br /> <br /> Parliament of Knives is written by the same guy who did the Werewolves series, which I also enjoyed. Not only does the game not brow beat you over the head by TELLING you how your character is supposed to be feeling about a particular situation / action (unlike New York), but the DLC also lets you join the Sabbat in one of the endings.<br /> <br /> <br /> New York, on the other hand, your choices do not matter. Even if you fuck up royal and fail to assemble a coterie, the game will still bail you out at the end when you get into trouble. It's railroaded to hell and back, as if you try to do something the Storyteller disapproves of, it will seize control of your character and force you back on track.<br /> <br /> The third game in the series is probably the worst, as I've seen people report about how it completely disregarded their choices made in previous chapters, in order to present a 'canon' route for its plot. Characters who had died in previous games suddenly coming back to life, as if nothing happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree that <i>Parliament of Knives</i> seems to be the best published to date and it's nice we can even cause the destruction of some high ranking Camarilla Cainites, that felt quite refreshing, especially since said cainite was an ass lol. Regarding Julian, yes, I wanted to kill him from the first time I saw him. He's disgusting, a fucking Gary Stu, stupid and repulsive. Damn, I hate that character so much that I realized I'm not playing <i>Night Road</i> again just because I don't want to deal with that piece of shit ever again. If <i>Night Road</i> didn't have him, it would be 100% better, no doubt.<br /> <br /> Regarding the <i>New York</i> series, I agree that our choices don't mean a damn thing, and the third one (<i>Reckoning of New York</i>) is VERY weak\u2014it\u2019s the one where our choices matter the <b>least</b>. I wanted to kill Thomas Arturo the moment I saw him; he's such an asshole. But at least he's nowhere near the level of garbage that is Julian Sim, and it's nice to see the Sheriff basically telling him to STFU for once lol. I liked Julia Sowinski, and <i>Shadows of New York</i> remains my favorite in the series; it feels like the only one where our <b>choices</b> <b>matter</b> a bit.<br /> <br /> As a general statement, I feel that in most of these games, Disciplines are rather weak, and it's often better to rely on regular Abilities. I was playing <i>Sins of the Sires</i>, and in this one specifically, vampires feel incredibly weak. There was a scene where I tried to stop a cop with a gun, and the game was like, &quot;you're no match for a gun.&quot; I was like, WTF!? Which Cainite is afraid of a mortal with a gun!? Even the lowest fledgling piece of horseshit of a cainite should be able to laugh at a pistol, especially since I had <b>Fortitude 3</b>! That made me lose it completely. Come on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T14:46:12-08:00","id":1557684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557674#post1557674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a general statement, I feel that in most of these games, Disciplines are rather weak, and it's often better to rely on regular Abilities. I was playing <i>Sins of the Sires</i>, and in this one specifically, vampires feel incredibly weak. There was a scene where I tried to stop a cop with a gun, and the game was like, &quot;you're no match for a gun.&quot; I was like, WTF!? Which Cainite is afraid of a mortal with a gun!? Even the lowest fledgling piece of horseshit of a cainite should be able to laugh at a pistol, especially since I had <b>Fortitude 3</b>! That made me lose it completely. Come on!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another perk in PoK's corner. It also remembers that <b>vampires have fucking super powers.</b> In nearly every other 5th edition set game I've come across, the Second Inquisition showing up is pretty much a death sentence for the vampires. They get caught with their pants down and have to flee the scene.<br /> <br /> But in Parliament, you end up making the SI look like a complete joke, as you tear your way through them.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to rebuy Nightroad, after seeing how the DLC has introduced almost every clan as a playable option now. Last time I played it, I believe I ended up diablerizing the final boss. Both for power, and because <i>&quot;fuck Julian.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------</i><br /> <br /> Speaking of Parliament of Knives, you might be interested in checking out Book of Hungry Names. I understand that at least one of the vampire characters (a Tremere, I think?) makes a crossover appearance, and is a prominent character in one of the DLC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T14:59:59-08:00","id":1557685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557674#post1557674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the <i>New York</i> series, I agree that our choices don't mean a damn thing, and the third one (<i>Reckoning of New York</i>) is VERY weak\u2014it\u2019s the one where our choices matter the <b>least</b>. I wanted to kill Thomas Arturo the moment I saw him; he's such an asshole. But at least he's nowhere near the level of garbage that is Julian Sim, and it's nice to see the Sheriff basically telling him to STFU for once lol. I liked Julia Sowinski, and <i>Shadows of New York</i> remains my favorite in the series; it feels like the only one where our <b>choices</b> <b>matter</b> a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, if I had my hands on a vial of Ravnos' blood, I would use it to mass embrace as many people as I could, and diablerize them while they were still delirious from the embrace. You get the benefits of eating a bunch of super low gens, without the risk of them taking control of your body.<br /> <br /> PLUS, 1st edition seemed to suggest that Ravnos may have actually been a surviving member of the 2nd generation. Which, if that is still true, means this plan could potentially make you a 3rd generation, without having to eat an actual antedeluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T15:04:27-08:00","id":1557686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557684#post1557684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's another perk in PoK's corner. It also remembers that <b>vampires have fucking super powers.</b> In nearly every other 5th edition set game I've come across, the Second Inquisition showing up is pretty much a death sentence for the vampires. They get caught with their pants down and have to flee the scene.<br /> <br /> But in Parliament, you end up making the SI look like a complete joke, as you tear your way through them.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> I'm tempted to rebuy Nightroad, after seeing how the DLC has introduced almost every clan as a playable option now. Last time I played it, I believe I ended up diablerizing the final boss. Both for power, and because <i>&quot;fuck Julian.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------</i><br /> <br /> Speaking of Parliament of Knives, you might be interested in checking out Book of Hungry Names. I understand that at least one of the vampire characters (a Tremere, I think?) makes a crossover appearance, and is a prominent character in one of the DLC's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, in Parliament of Knives we actually feel like vampires and that our powers and choices matter. Nightroad is good and I really like some characters like the Gangrel Prince, for instance. But just remembring Julian kills my enthusiasm to play it again.<br /> <br /> This Book of Hungry Names is on my radar, but can we play with this Vampire or is he just an important NPC? I'm currently playing Heart of the Forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T15:26:47-08:00","id":1557689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415331-vampire-the-masquerade-night-road-discussion-thread?p=1557686#post1557686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, in Parliament of Knives we actually feel like vampires and that our powers and choices matter. Nightroad is good and I really like some characters like the Gangrel Prince, for instance. But just remembring Julian kills my enthusiasm to play it again.<br /> <br /> This Book of Hungry Names is on my radar, but can we play with this Vampire or is he just an important NPC? I'm currently playing Heart of the Forest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not gotten to that point in the DLC yet, so I can't say for sure. But I believe he is the main villain of the DLC side quest.<br /> <br /> Book of Hungry Names is definitely worth the money. In terms of word count, the game is stated to be 2 - 3x longer than Lord of the Rings. So you'll definitely have a lot of play time available.<br /> <br /> With all the DLC included, the game has all the playable 5th edition Tribes. The only ones who aren't available of <b>Black Spirals</b> and <b>Get of Fenris...</b><br /> <br /> ~sigh, yes... they presented the Get as being white supremacists in this game.<br /> <br /> <br /> But I'm willing to overlook that, since you can still form a truce with them to help take down a powerful Fomori at some point.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: My first playthrough was a <b>Shadow Lord</b>, my second was <b>Silver Fang</b>, and now I'm on my third as a <b>Red Talon</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 01-16-2026, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}